1
00:00:01,335 --> 00:00:03,031
♪♪

2
00:01:14,741 --> 00:01:17,506
<i>From the fire ravaged
community of Southgate.</i>

3
00:01:17,644 --> 00:01:20,239
<i>For most of Atlanta,
this day started out</i>

4
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:22,747
<i>with the promise of a
clear and sunny spring day.</i>

5
00:01:22,883 --> 00:01:25,910
<i>But in the Southgate community,
that calm was shattered</i>

6
00:01:26,053 --> 00:01:28,284
<i>by the scream of fire
trucks and ambulances</i>

7
00:01:28,422 --> 00:01:31,790
<i>when a four-alarm fire
erupted just hours before dawn.</i>

8
00:01:31,925 --> 00:01:35,259
<i>Engine companies from all over
the city raced to the scene of the fire</i>

9
00:01:35,395 --> 00:01:38,888
<i>but sadly were not able to
prevent extensive property damage.</i>

10
00:01:39,032 --> 00:01:41,592
<i>The pictures of devastation
that you are seeing</i>

11
00:01:41,735 --> 00:01:45,365
<i>are the first to be authorized for
release by the police and fire departments,</i>

12
00:01:45,505 --> 00:01:48,475
<i>due to unusually tight
security in the area.</i>

13
00:01:48,609 --> 00:01:53,206
<i>This is the third large-scale fire in
the Southgate area in the last month.</i>

14
00:01:53,347 --> 00:01:57,114
<i>And like the previous cases,
this fire spread extremely quickly,</i>

15
00:01:57,250 --> 00:02:00,049
<i>hopping from house to
house with terrifying speed.</i>

16
00:02:00,187 --> 00:02:04,488
<i>Many residents of the area were forced
to flee, leaving all possessions behind.</i>

17
00:02:04,625 --> 00:02:09,757
<i>Most of the residents we were able to
speak with were still in a state of shock.</i>

18
00:02:09,896 --> 00:02:13,458
<i>Several others were undergoing
treatment at the Munson Memorial Hospital</i>

19
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:17,128
<i>for symptoms of shock, smoke
inhalation, and minor injuries.</i>

20
00:02:17,270 --> 00:02:22,140
<i>Many expressed anger at what they
called outside influences and gangs,</i>

21
00:02:22,275 --> 00:02:24,938
<i>whom they blamed for
this spate of recent fires.</i>

22
00:02:25,078 --> 00:02:28,947
<i>A number of residents expressed their
intention to leave the area permanently.</i>

23
00:02:29,082 --> 00:02:32,348
<i>Police officials have
cordoned off an entire area...</i>

24
00:02:42,362 --> 00:02:44,490
It pains me to say
this, Your Honor,

25
00:02:44,631 --> 00:02:48,796
but your ruling
clearly indicates to me

26
00:02:48,935 --> 00:02:51,632
that you are a jackass.

27
00:02:51,772 --> 00:02:53,934
- You said that to his face?
- Right to his face.

28
00:02:54,074 --> 00:02:55,074
My gosh, what did he do?

29
00:02:55,175 --> 00:02:57,440
Oh, he turned as
red as a radish.

30
00:02:57,577 --> 00:02:58,704
He charged me with contempt,

31
00:02:58,845 --> 00:03:00,575
threw me in the
hoosegow for the night,

32
00:03:00,714 --> 00:03:02,012
and reversed his ruling.

33
00:03:02,149 --> 00:03:04,311
- No kidding.
- No kidding.

34
00:03:05,652 --> 00:03:09,089
Is it okay to say
"jackass" on TV?

35
00:03:09,222 --> 00:03:10,246
Are you kidding?

36
00:03:10,390 --> 00:03:13,622
Ever since those confirmation
hearings, you can say practically anything.

37
00:03:14,695 --> 00:03:16,391
Jackass, jackass, jackass.

38
00:03:17,698 --> 00:03:20,600
Okay, let's talk about
the Peabody case.

39
00:03:20,734 --> 00:03:21,929
The who case?

40
00:03:22,069 --> 00:03:24,800
The Professor Peabody
triple murder case?

41
00:03:26,406 --> 00:03:29,137
You know, the one where
you represented the geneticist

42
00:03:29,276 --> 00:03:31,472
who was trying to breed
the world's first talking dog?

43
00:03:32,713 --> 00:03:33,737
You don't remember?

44
00:03:35,549 --> 00:03:38,041
No, and I'm sure I would.

45
00:03:39,252 --> 00:03:43,553
<i>Let's talk about the time you
represented those two Russian spies, then.</i>

46
00:03:43,690 --> 00:03:45,386
<i>Russian spies?</i>

47
00:03:45,525 --> 00:03:47,153
<i>Yeah... Boris and Natasha.</i>

48
00:03:47,294 --> 00:03:48,956
<i>Last name Badenov.</i>

49
00:03:50,997 --> 00:03:53,125
<i>- I don't remember them, either.</i>
- Oh, no.

50
00:03:53,266 --> 00:03:54,986
<i>They were accused of
murdering two people...</i>

51
00:03:55,102 --> 00:03:57,662
<i>An R. J. Squirrel
and a B. W. Moose.</i>

52
00:03:59,439 --> 00:04:00,964
<i>Moose and Squirrel?</i>

53
00:04:01,108 --> 00:04:02,108
<i>Yes.</i>

54
00:04:03,276 --> 00:04:04,505
<i>Wait a minute...</i>

55
00:04:05,512 --> 00:04:07,003
<i>B. W. Moose?</i>

56
00:04:07,147 --> 00:04:09,480
<i>Okay. Cut. Damn it.</i>

57
00:04:11,151 --> 00:04:12,380
Doug.

58
00:04:15,455 --> 00:04:17,788
You made me look like a
jackass in front of Ben Matlock.

59
00:04:17,924 --> 00:04:19,984
- Oh, relax, Bill, it's a joke.
- Damn you.

60
00:04:22,596 --> 00:04:23,928
Where's your sense of humor?

61
00:04:24,064 --> 00:04:25,498
You don't get it, Doug.

62
00:04:25,632 --> 00:04:26,998
You and your practical jokes

63
00:04:27,134 --> 00:04:29,895
are going to ruin credibility of
this station's entire news operation.

64
00:04:30,003 --> 00:04:33,735
If you checked out your stories, I
wouldn't have been able to trick you.

65
00:04:33,874 --> 00:04:35,365
But you don't, so I did.

66
00:04:35,509 --> 00:04:39,037
Doug, don't do that again.

67
00:04:39,179 --> 00:04:40,670
Okay.

68
00:04:40,814 --> 00:04:42,544
Now get back to work.

69
00:04:45,519 --> 00:04:48,765
<i>The contents of the overturned
truck caught fire immediately,</i>

70
00:04:48,789 --> 00:04:52,226
<i>but the driver was able to
escape with only minor injuries.</i>

71
00:04:52,359 --> 00:04:53,736
<i>In Washington...</i>

72
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:55,271
<i>the President, at a
fund-raising event,</i>

73
00:04:55,295 --> 00:04:56,786
<i>reiterated his desire to...</i>

74
00:04:56,930 --> 00:04:58,193
Come in. Close the door.

75
00:04:58,331 --> 00:05:00,459
<i>Provision he recommended
only weeks ago.</i>

76
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:03,502
<i>The President proposed
to cut the capital gains tax...</i>

77
00:05:03,637 --> 00:05:05,299
The latest audience research.

78
00:05:05,438 --> 00:05:08,237
Diane's ratings are
sinking like the <i>Titanic.</i>

79
00:05:08,375 --> 00:05:10,241
<i>Modified so that upper income...</i>

80
00:05:10,377 --> 00:05:13,074
Maybe if we team her up with
somebody young and fresh.

81
00:05:13,213 --> 00:05:15,307
Dump her.

82
00:05:15,448 --> 00:05:17,644
She's been with the
station more than 12 years.

83
00:05:17,784 --> 00:05:21,551
Well, you're going to have
to sooner or later, Howard.

84
00:05:21,688 --> 00:05:23,589
Get some new blood. Dump her.

85
00:05:23,723 --> 00:05:25,935
A woman her age in this
business... What's she going to do?

86
00:05:25,959 --> 00:05:30,420
If there's one thing this lady
knows how to do, it's land on her feet.

87
00:05:30,564 --> 00:05:32,260
<i>Locally, after a
three-day hiatus,</i>

88
00:05:32,399 --> 00:05:34,079
<i>the zoning commission
reassembles tomorrow.</i>

89
00:05:34,201 --> 00:05:35,294
<i>When it convenes,</i>

90
00:05:35,435 --> 00:05:38,894
<i>the commission will consider rezoning
an eight-mile stretch of farmland</i>

91
00:05:39,039 --> 00:05:42,134
<i>located between state route
96 and McKenzie Highway</i>

92
00:05:42,275 --> 00:05:46,371
<i>to allow for the development of
high-density, multi-family dwellings.</i>

93
00:05:47,547 --> 00:05:51,712
I can no longer sit idly by and watch
as thousands of my fellow citizens

94
00:05:51,852 --> 00:05:57,484
fall victim to political inertia,
ineptitude, and just plain apathy.

95
00:05:57,624 --> 00:05:59,957
I, therefore, hereby declare
that as of this moment

96
00:06:00,093 --> 00:06:02,585
I seek to be the next
duly-elected representative

97
00:06:02,729 --> 00:06:05,460
of the 11th Congressional
District of the great state of Georgia.

98
00:06:08,101 --> 00:06:09,330
Anybody have any questions?

99
00:06:09,469 --> 00:06:11,529
- Mr. Bevins!
- Right here!

100
00:06:12,906 --> 00:06:16,308
Will yours be a positive
or a negative campaign?

101
00:06:16,443 --> 00:06:18,963
Well, let's just say I owe it to
the good citizens of this state

102
00:06:19,079 --> 00:06:21,173
to do whatever it takes
to beat the incumbent.

103
00:06:21,314 --> 00:06:22,942
- Here.
- Yes.

104
00:06:23,083 --> 00:06:24,574
How do you respond
to the charges

105
00:06:24,718 --> 00:06:26,846
the Atlanta Nature Society
has leveled against you?

106
00:06:26,987 --> 00:06:29,422
The Atlanta Nature Society?

107
00:06:29,556 --> 00:06:33,084
They released a statement today
charging you with being anti-environment.

108
00:06:33,226 --> 00:06:35,957
That's ridiculous. If anything, I'm
just the opposite. Next question.

109
00:06:36,096 --> 00:06:38,190
It's right here in their
press release, Mr. Bevins.

110
00:06:38,331 --> 00:06:41,267
They say you're so deeply indebted
to big business and heavy industry

111
00:06:41,401 --> 00:06:44,428
that you can't possibly
address environmental issues

112
00:06:44,571 --> 00:06:46,005
with any degree of objectivity.

113
00:06:46,139 --> 00:06:48,131
Mr. Finley, that is slander.

114
00:06:48,275 --> 00:06:51,074
I'm simply repeating what
is in this press release.

115
00:06:51,211 --> 00:06:53,043
Everyone in this
room got one of these.

116
00:06:55,815 --> 00:06:58,546
You've been had again, Billy.

117
00:07:00,720 --> 00:07:02,552
- Mr. Bevins?
- Mr. Bevins!

118
00:07:22,842 --> 00:07:24,834
Are you happy now? I'm fired.

119
00:07:24,978 --> 00:07:26,879
I had nothing to do
with that press release.

120
00:07:27,013 --> 00:07:29,453
The hell you didn't. You dummied
it up and left it on my desk.

121
00:07:29,516 --> 00:07:32,008
It was somebody
else this time, not me.

122
00:07:32,152 --> 00:07:33,152
Yeah, Doug.

123
00:07:33,219 --> 00:07:37,418
Well, just remember, what
goes around comes around.

124
00:07:41,194 --> 00:07:43,720
Doug, can I see you a minute?

125
00:07:51,171 --> 00:07:55,404
Scout's honor, Howard. I had
nothing to do with that Bevins fiasco.

126
00:07:55,542 --> 00:07:58,842
Good. The last thing I want is to
have to fire someone else around here.

127
00:08:00,613 --> 00:08:03,173
If the kid had just
made one phone call,

128
00:08:03,316 --> 00:08:05,547
he'd have known that that
press release was a phony.

129
00:08:05,685 --> 00:08:08,814
But, as usual, he just barged straight
ahead without checking his facts.

130
00:08:08,955 --> 00:08:11,167
I know. I know. That's not what
I wanted to talk to you about.

131
00:08:11,191 --> 00:08:13,456
I just got a call from the
zoning commissioner.

132
00:08:13,593 --> 00:08:17,052
We got our facts wrong on
a story we aired last night...

133
00:08:17,197 --> 00:08:20,964
The one about the proposed rezoning
of some farmland south of Route 96.

134
00:08:21,101 --> 00:08:23,764
We said the property goes all
the way to McKenzie Highway.

135
00:08:23,903 --> 00:08:24,996
It doesn't.

136
00:08:25,138 --> 00:08:26,333
Is that a big deal?

137
00:08:26,473 --> 00:08:28,305
It is to Nelson Addleson.

138
00:08:28,441 --> 00:08:31,900
He owns that property, and it
quadrupled in value overnight.

139
00:08:32,045 --> 00:08:34,310
- Wow.
- A bunch of speculators snapped it up.

140
00:08:34,447 --> 00:08:37,576
Addleson made a killing, which
really fried the commissioner's <i>frijoles.</i>

141
00:08:37,717 --> 00:08:39,413
He hates Nelson Addleson's guts.

142
00:08:39,552 --> 00:08:43,114
Well, I don't know how it
happened, but I'll find out.

143
00:08:43,256 --> 00:08:44,588
Do that.

144
00:08:44,724 --> 00:08:48,593
And run a correction and an apology
at the top of tonight's broadcast.

145
00:08:48,728 --> 00:08:50,458
You got it.

146
00:09:01,508 --> 00:09:03,443
It won't be ready by
the broadcast tonight.

147
00:09:03,576 --> 00:09:05,204
They're working on
it down in Studio 7.

148
00:09:05,345 --> 00:09:06,369
Got it.

149
00:09:12,952 --> 00:09:15,421
You, my lady, are
about to get canned.

150
00:09:16,990 --> 00:09:20,017
I figured. My numbers are down.

151
00:09:20,160 --> 00:09:21,219
Did Howard tell you?

152
00:09:21,361 --> 00:09:23,626
Yeah, Howard.

153
00:09:25,565 --> 00:09:28,091
He knows about the little gaffe
you made on the air last night.

154
00:09:28,234 --> 00:09:30,863
The zoning commissioner called.

155
00:09:31,004 --> 00:09:34,406
And he's found out about the
killing that Nelson's making.

156
00:09:34,541 --> 00:09:37,534
He wants us to broadcast
a correction ASAP.

157
00:09:37,677 --> 00:09:40,340
- Are we going to?
- In a day or two.

158
00:09:40,480 --> 00:09:43,814
The longer we wait, the
more money we make.

159
00:09:46,553 --> 00:09:50,456
I did what you said... set up two
accounts at the Royal Bank of Bermuda.

160
00:09:50,590 --> 00:09:55,790
Down there, you are now known as
Kevin Galloway, and I'm Vicky Davis.

161
00:09:55,929 --> 00:09:57,625
Cute.

162
00:09:57,764 --> 00:10:01,758
How are you going
to explain the gaffe?

163
00:10:01,901 --> 00:10:03,961
One of our writers
got his facts wrong.

164
00:10:04,104 --> 00:10:05,572
It happens all the time.

165
00:10:06,773 --> 00:10:08,503
I hope we get away with it.

166
00:10:08,641 --> 00:10:10,619
Hey, you're the one that
cut yourself in on this deal.

167
00:10:10,643 --> 00:10:13,442
Yeah. When I found out
what you two were up to,

168
00:10:13,580 --> 00:10:16,607
I'm sure I should have just
blown the whistle on you then.

169
00:10:16,749 --> 00:10:17,749
Hey, come on.

170
00:10:17,784 --> 00:10:21,778
Unemployment can
be fun if you're rich.

171
00:10:34,234 --> 00:10:35,862
Nelson.

172
00:10:36,002 --> 00:10:37,436
Nelson.

173
00:10:37,570 --> 00:10:39,539
Nelson, no, you listen to me.

174
00:10:40,607 --> 00:10:42,132
Now, we've stalled long enough.

175
00:10:42,275 --> 00:10:45,439
Okay, one more
day, but that's it.

176
00:10:49,849 --> 00:10:53,149
Not that fellow who
interviewed me the other day?

177
00:10:53,286 --> 00:10:55,949
No, no, no. That was
Bill Finley. I fired him.

178
00:10:56,089 --> 00:10:59,287
Why? Because of that
Rocky Bullwinkle business?

179
00:10:59,425 --> 00:11:02,054
I fired him because there's
so much air between his ears,

180
00:11:02,195 --> 00:11:04,255
- it's a wonder he doesn't float away.
- Hmm.

181
00:11:04,397 --> 00:11:06,423
I'm talking about the
producer, Doug Levitt.

182
00:11:06,566 --> 00:11:08,000
Oh. Here.

183
00:11:08,134 --> 00:11:09,134
Thank you.

184
00:11:09,235 --> 00:11:10,601
- Popcorn?
- No.

185
00:11:10,737 --> 00:11:12,672
It's good. From a
health food store.

186
00:11:12,805 --> 00:11:14,000
No.

187
00:11:14,140 --> 00:11:15,540
Moves everything around.

188
00:11:17,177 --> 00:11:18,577
No.

189
00:11:19,879 --> 00:11:21,438
So what did this...
What's his name?

190
00:11:21,581 --> 00:11:23,140
- Levitt.
- Levitt. What did he do?

191
00:11:23,283 --> 00:11:25,479
Two nights ago, we aired a story

192
00:11:25,618 --> 00:11:28,782
that made it sound like some
worthless land was about to be rezoned

193
00:11:28,922 --> 00:11:30,686
for a big residential
development.

194
00:11:30,823 --> 00:11:32,621
As it turns out, the
story wasn't true.

195
00:11:32,759 --> 00:11:35,524
But in the meantime, the
value of the land quadrupled,

196
00:11:35,662 --> 00:11:38,757
and Nelson Addleson made a
fortune selling it to speculators.

197
00:11:38,898 --> 00:11:42,665
I think Doug falsified the story because
he and Nelson Addleson are in cahoots.

198
00:11:42,802 --> 00:11:44,464
Can you prove that?

199
00:11:44,604 --> 00:11:46,004
That's why I'm
here. You tell me.

200
00:11:46,139 --> 00:11:49,200
Today I overheard part of
a telephone conversation

201
00:11:49,342 --> 00:11:51,538
between Doug Levitt
and Nelson Addleson,

202
00:11:51,678 --> 00:11:53,613
so I checked Doug's
car phone bills.

203
00:11:53,746 --> 00:11:56,272
The station pays them,
so he always turns them in.

204
00:11:56,416 --> 00:11:57,475
Huh.

205
00:11:59,886 --> 00:12:04,381
Kind of foolish... Dumb if
he's up to something, isn't it?

206
00:12:04,524 --> 00:12:09,428
Look at that... nine calls in the
past two weeks to Nelson Addleson.

207
00:12:09,562 --> 00:12:13,090
So can I nail the little
weasel to the wall or what?

208
00:12:13,233 --> 00:12:14,895
Did you talk to him?

209
00:12:15,034 --> 00:12:16,034
No.

210
00:12:16,102 --> 00:12:19,163
Why don't you talk to him? Maybe
he's got a logical explanation.

211
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:28,480
Sit down.

212
00:12:33,620 --> 00:12:36,522
What's the nature of your
relationship to Nelson Addleson?

213
00:12:37,757 --> 00:12:40,727
I don't have a relationship
with Nelson Addleson.

214
00:12:40,860 --> 00:12:42,886
You never see him?
You never talk to him?

215
00:12:43,029 --> 00:12:44,190
No. Why would I?

216
00:12:47,634 --> 00:12:48,693
You're fired, Doug.

217
00:12:48,835 --> 00:12:51,430
I want your desk cleared
out by the end of the day.

218
00:12:52,472 --> 00:12:54,634
- Wait a minute...
- I may press charges, I may not,

219
00:12:54,774 --> 00:12:56,299
depending upon
what the attorneys say.

220
00:12:56,442 --> 00:12:59,503
But in any case, you just looked
me straight in the eye and lied to me.

221
00:12:59,646 --> 00:13:02,946
I won't have liars working
for me. Now get out.

222
00:13:15,762 --> 00:13:16,923
Hey, Doug?

223
00:13:33,613 --> 00:13:35,013
You look awful.

224
00:13:35,148 --> 00:13:36,446
What happened?

225
00:13:36,582 --> 00:13:38,483
I got the ax.

226
00:13:38,618 --> 00:13:40,814
Ah, coffee.

227
00:13:40,953 --> 00:13:43,388
Did it have anything to
do with Nelson Addleson?

228
00:13:43,523 --> 00:13:48,018
Yeah. Yeah. Howard found out.

229
00:13:48,161 --> 00:13:50,630
Oh, my God.

230
00:13:50,763 --> 00:13:53,961
Not about you...
at least not yet.

231
00:13:55,134 --> 00:13:57,262
What the hell is that
supposed to mean?

232
00:13:57,403 --> 00:14:01,932
Well, Howard might
decide to press charges.

233
00:14:02,075 --> 00:14:04,977
If I stand trial, anything
might come out.

234
00:14:06,245 --> 00:14:08,180
What is that?
Some kind of threat?

235
00:14:08,314 --> 00:14:10,340
No, of course not. It's
just a statement of fact.

236
00:14:10,483 --> 00:14:12,611
Besides, what do you care?

237
00:14:12,752 --> 00:14:15,119
All this was about
to end anyway.

238
00:14:15,254 --> 00:14:17,519
Or were you just worried
about your money?

239
00:14:17,657 --> 00:14:19,023
Well, aren't you?

240
00:14:23,563 --> 00:14:25,054
What's this?

241
00:14:25,198 --> 00:14:28,930
Uh, it was mixed in with all the
stuff I brought home from work.

242
00:14:29,068 --> 00:14:30,348
I don't know where it came from.

243
00:14:30,470 --> 00:14:32,336
You played that
trick on Bill Finley.

244
00:14:32,472 --> 00:14:33,872
No, I didn't.

245
00:14:34,006 --> 00:14:37,272
Practical jokes aren't
my style, and you know it.

246
00:14:37,410 --> 00:14:39,470
Uh-huh.

247
00:14:39,612 --> 00:14:42,673
Well, I'd get out
of town for a while,

248
00:14:42,815 --> 00:14:46,513
but I don't want to give Nelson
an excuse not to pay me my cut.

249
00:14:46,652 --> 00:14:51,420
Well, I could go to Nelson and ask
him for your share as well as my own

250
00:14:51,557 --> 00:14:53,355
and then wire it
to you in Bermuda.

251
00:14:53,493 --> 00:14:57,726
No. No. First I get my money,
then I get out of the country.

252
00:14:57,864 --> 00:15:00,264
Then why can't I meet you
somewhere and give it to you there?

253
00:15:00,366 --> 00:15:02,699
Your cottage at Sidney Lake?

254
00:15:02,835 --> 00:15:05,532
- When?
- Tuesday afternoon.

255
00:15:06,706 --> 00:15:07,706
3.

256
00:15:08,708 --> 00:15:10,677
Thank you, Diane.

257
00:15:10,810 --> 00:15:12,745
I appreciate it.

258
00:17:31,450 --> 00:17:33,544
Would you mind turning around?

259
00:17:34,554 --> 00:17:35,715
What?

260
00:17:35,855 --> 00:17:38,415
I just want to get a look at
you. Please, take off your hat.

261
00:17:39,592 --> 00:17:40,821
You a cop?

262
00:17:40,960 --> 00:17:42,861
Would you take off your hat?

263
00:17:49,035 --> 00:17:52,233
How'd you like to make a couple
of hundred bucks for doing nothing?

264
00:17:53,706 --> 00:17:54,833
Yeah.

265
00:19:59,065 --> 00:20:00,260
<i>Good evening, everyone.</i>

266
00:20:00,399 --> 00:20:01,662
<i>At the top of tonight's news,</i>

267
00:20:01,801 --> 00:20:05,568
<i>a story that has sent shockwaves
through the local broadcasting community.</i>

268
00:20:05,705 --> 00:20:10,507
<i>Doug Levitt, former producer of the</i>
5:00 News Hour <i>here at WDRN-TV</i>

269
00:20:10,643 --> 00:20:13,842
<i>died earlier this
afternoon in an explosion</i>

270
00:20:13,866 --> 00:20:17,015
<i>that destroyed his
cottage at Sidney Lake.</i>

271
00:20:17,149 --> 00:20:19,516
<i>Police have just identified
the charred remains</i>

272
00:20:19,652 --> 00:20:21,382
<i>found at the scene
through dental records</i>

273
00:20:21,520 --> 00:20:24,080
<i>and by tracing jewelry
the victim was wearing.</i>

274
00:20:24,223 --> 00:20:28,388
<i>They say it appears that the explosion
was the result of a remote-controlled bomb,</i>

275
00:20:28,527 --> 00:20:31,429
<i>which means they are
treating this case as a homicide.</i>

276
00:20:31,564 --> 00:20:34,432
<i>The police have
arrested Bill Finley,</i>

277
00:20:34,567 --> 00:20:38,334
<i>a former station employee
who was fired last week.</i>

278
00:20:47,880 --> 00:20:50,611
Bail will be set at $200,000.

279
00:20:50,750 --> 00:20:53,948
Please see the cashier on the
second floor of the West Wing.

280
00:20:54,086 --> 00:20:55,884
Where am I supposed
to get $200,000?

281
00:20:56,021 --> 00:20:57,319
It will be taken care of.

282
00:20:57,456 --> 00:20:59,391
You're paying for my
lawyer and my bail?

283
00:20:59,525 --> 00:21:01,892
It's as clear as the nose on
my face you're innocent, Bill.

284
00:21:02,027 --> 00:21:05,267
And I feel like this is all my fault. If I
hadn't fired you, you wouldn't be here.

285
00:21:06,365 --> 00:21:08,300
Next case.

286
00:21:09,301 --> 00:21:11,395
<i>The People vs. Callahan...</i>

287
00:21:11,537 --> 00:21:12,561
What do you think?

288
00:21:12,705 --> 00:21:15,174
Well, I've got my
work cut out for me.

289
00:21:15,307 --> 00:21:18,766
I mean, the police found that
detonator in your garbage can.

290
00:21:18,911 --> 00:21:20,255
Anybody could
have put that there.

291
00:21:20,279 --> 00:21:23,716
Yeah. And the tire tracks
at the scene didn't help.

292
00:21:23,849 --> 00:21:26,546
Come on, a lot of people
drive the same kind of car I do.

293
00:21:26,685 --> 00:21:29,655
If you had an alibi, it would
help. That's all I'm saying.

294
00:21:29,789 --> 00:21:32,251
I told you, I was at
home working on a book

295
00:21:32,275 --> 00:21:34,818
that is going to blow
the lid off this town.

296
00:21:34,960 --> 00:21:36,600
You uncovered some
corruption in Atlanta?

297
00:21:36,695 --> 00:21:39,028
Well, I'm working on it.

298
00:21:40,166 --> 00:21:41,657
What's next?

299
00:21:41,801 --> 00:21:44,293
Well, I guess I'll go
see Nelson Addleson.

300
00:21:44,436 --> 00:21:46,098
- Let's go.
- No.

301
00:21:46,238 --> 00:21:47,501
No, no, no, no.

302
00:21:47,640 --> 00:21:48,717
You go home and stay there.

303
00:21:48,741 --> 00:21:51,233
Ben, I want to question him.

304
00:21:51,377 --> 00:21:52,377
No. No. Right?

305
00:21:52,511 --> 00:21:55,310
Go home and work on your book.

306
00:21:55,447 --> 00:21:56,915
Go.

307
00:22:06,225 --> 00:22:08,160
Are you sure you won't
join me, Mr. Matlock?

308
00:22:08,294 --> 00:22:11,628
It isn't just any scotch...
Flintrock. It's over 40 years old.

309
00:22:11,764 --> 00:22:12,823
Oh, no, thanks.

310
00:22:12,965 --> 00:22:17,027
That stuff all tastes
like lighter fluid to me.

311
00:22:17,169 --> 00:22:20,401
So what is this about?

312
00:22:21,407 --> 00:22:25,811
Well, it's about all
those phone calls

313
00:22:25,945 --> 00:22:28,744
Doug Levitt made to
you just before he died.

314
00:22:28,881 --> 00:22:32,079
Is there a law against
calling a friend?

315
00:22:32,218 --> 00:22:33,914
You and he were friends?

316
00:22:34,053 --> 00:22:35,453
Yes.

317
00:22:35,588 --> 00:22:38,353
He told Howard Price
he didn't know you.

318
00:22:38,490 --> 00:22:39,583
Really?

319
00:22:39,725 --> 00:22:41,489
I wonder why he did that.

320
00:22:41,627 --> 00:22:43,960
Howard's sure that it
had something to do

321
00:22:44,096 --> 00:22:49,399
with that false information
broadcast on Doug Levitt's news show.

322
00:22:49,535 --> 00:22:54,235
You know, that stuff about all
that farmland south of Route 96

323
00:22:54,373 --> 00:22:56,308
that was supposedly
up for rezoning.

324
00:22:56,442 --> 00:22:57,774
Yeah, of course.

325
00:22:59,845 --> 00:23:02,371
The station made a mistake,
and you made a killing.

326
00:23:02,514 --> 00:23:05,109
Yeah. Well, what
was I supposed to do?

327
00:23:05,251 --> 00:23:07,880
This is America. If something
like that happens, you go with it.

328
00:23:08,020 --> 00:23:09,044
Yeah.

329
00:23:10,656 --> 00:23:13,490
So Doug Levitt's phone
calls had nothing to do with it.

330
00:23:13,626 --> 00:23:14,719
No, of course not.

331
00:23:14,860 --> 00:23:16,829
What are you trying to say?

332
00:23:16,962 --> 00:23:19,022
That he and I were some
kind of co-conspirators?

333
00:23:19,164 --> 00:23:23,966
I'm just trying to figure out
why he lied about knowing you.

334
00:23:24,103 --> 00:23:27,870
With him gone, it's
anybody's guess.

335
00:23:29,008 --> 00:23:33,343
You know, there's a fine line
between speculation and libel,

336
00:23:33,479 --> 00:23:35,243
and my lawyers,
they know where it is.

337
00:23:35,381 --> 00:23:37,816
Yeah, I imagine they do.

338
00:23:37,950 --> 00:23:41,216
But since I'm so close
to that fine line anyhow,

339
00:23:41,353 --> 00:23:43,913
how about telling me where
you were the afternoon he died?

340
00:23:49,795 --> 00:23:52,196
I was with a woman
named Jody Pfeiffer.

341
00:23:52,331 --> 00:23:53,697
Here's her phone number.

342
00:23:57,169 --> 00:23:59,604
I'd appreciate your
keeping that under your hat.

343
00:23:59,738 --> 00:24:05,871
It wasn't exactly a business
meeting, and I'm not exactly single.

344
00:24:06,011 --> 00:24:08,207
Oh.

345
00:24:09,315 --> 00:24:12,479
You like walking
those fine lines, too.

346
00:25:00,432 --> 00:25:02,526
Do you always run
through stop signs?

347
00:25:02,668 --> 00:25:04,762
What stop sign?

348
00:25:04,903 --> 00:25:06,132
Back there, 100 feet.

349
00:25:06,271 --> 00:25:08,467
Where? Do you mind
if I get out of the car?

350
00:25:08,607 --> 00:25:10,633
Just keep your hands
where I can see them, sir.

351
00:25:12,811 --> 00:25:13,904
Where is it?

352
00:25:17,549 --> 00:25:19,950
There's a bush in
front of that stop sign.

353
00:25:20,085 --> 00:25:21,085
I didn't see it.

354
00:25:21,153 --> 00:25:22,451
You can see enough of it.

355
00:25:22,588 --> 00:25:24,420
How much is that ticket?

356
00:25:24,556 --> 00:25:26,354
Sixty-one dollars.

357
00:25:26,492 --> 00:25:27,721
Sign here, please.

358
00:25:28,727 --> 00:25:31,287
That stop sign's
obscured. I won't pay it.

359
00:25:31,430 --> 00:25:33,490
That's up to you,
sir. Pay it or fight it.

360
00:25:33,632 --> 00:25:34,632
Sign here.

361
00:25:36,702 --> 00:25:39,103
Only eight days to
prepare my case?

362
00:25:39,238 --> 00:25:41,036
Prepare your ca...

363
00:25:41,173 --> 00:25:43,699
You're going to a
lot of trouble for $61.

364
00:25:43,842 --> 00:25:45,572
It's the principle.

365
00:25:46,645 --> 00:25:48,637
Sure.

366
00:25:56,722 --> 00:25:58,816
Finally. Come on in.

367
00:25:58,957 --> 00:26:00,721
What's up?

368
00:26:00,859 --> 00:26:02,088
Look at this.

369
00:26:02,227 --> 00:26:05,356
Somebody found it in Diane
Becker's office this morning.

370
00:26:12,004 --> 00:26:15,133
I don't understand.
Somebody found this in here?

371
00:26:15,274 --> 00:26:19,712
Mr. Price's assistant found it when
she dropped the ratings off this morning.

372
00:26:19,845 --> 00:26:21,973
I don't know anything about it.

373
00:26:22,114 --> 00:26:26,552
It kind of looks like you pulled that prank
on Bill Finley, knowing he'd be fired.

374
00:26:26,685 --> 00:26:29,655
Oh. No, I did no such thing.

375
00:26:29,788 --> 00:26:32,622
I hate practical
jokes. Ask anybody.

376
00:26:32,758 --> 00:26:34,318
Well, maybe you
didn't do it as a joke.

377
00:26:34,393 --> 00:26:36,453
Maybe you did it
knowing for sure

378
00:26:36,595 --> 00:26:39,929
that Bill would be fired and would
automatically blame Doug Levitt.

379
00:26:40,065 --> 00:26:43,695
What are you saying?
That I tried to frame him?

380
00:26:43,836 --> 00:26:46,704
That I really killed Doug?

381
00:26:46,839 --> 00:26:49,035
I'm just commenting
on the way things look.

382
00:26:49,174 --> 00:26:52,201
I'm busy trying to make an
honest living here. All right?

383
00:26:52,344 --> 00:26:55,075
How about the afternoon of the
murder? Were you busy then?

384
00:26:55,214 --> 00:26:59,743
I was right here editing
copy. Again, just ask anybody.

385
00:26:59,885 --> 00:27:01,217
Okay.

386
00:27:03,522 --> 00:27:09,553
Uh, was your door
open or closed?

387
00:27:09,695 --> 00:27:11,391
Closed.

388
00:27:17,603 --> 00:27:19,663
- Diane faked that press release?
- Maybe.

389
00:27:19,805 --> 00:27:23,367
Diane doesn't play practical jokes.
That's the only thing I like about her.

390
00:27:23,509 --> 00:27:25,171
Maybe it wasn't
a practical joke.

391
00:27:25,310 --> 00:27:28,439
Maybe she knew you'd get
fired and blow up at Doug Levitt.

392
00:27:28,580 --> 00:27:29,843
Maybe she was setting you up.

393
00:27:29,982 --> 00:27:32,213
You mean Diane killed Doug?

394
00:27:32,351 --> 00:27:33,819
Did she have any reason?

395
00:27:33,952 --> 00:27:37,445
Not that I know of. They
seemed to get along.

396
00:27:37,589 --> 00:27:39,251
What now?

397
00:27:39,391 --> 00:27:41,917
Well, I'll go over
to Doug's place

398
00:27:42,060 --> 00:27:45,963
and see if I can dig up some
connection between the two of them.

399
00:27:46,098 --> 00:27:48,033
I'll go with you.
Let me get my stuff.

400
00:27:48,167 --> 00:27:50,227
No. No, no, no, no, no.

401
00:27:50,369 --> 00:27:54,568
I know you've got that magnifying
glass and fingerprint set and stuff, Bill,

402
00:27:54,706 --> 00:27:56,937
but you'd better
work on your book.

403
00:27:57,075 --> 00:27:58,873
Somebody framed me, Ben.

404
00:27:59,011 --> 00:28:01,091
You don't expect me to just
sit on my thumbs, do you?

405
00:28:01,213 --> 00:28:02,237
Yeah.

406
00:28:05,717 --> 00:28:08,084
What I don't understand
is why a bomb?

407
00:28:08,220 --> 00:28:09,518
Why didn't she just shoot him?

408
00:28:09,655 --> 00:28:11,375
She's trying to
frame Bill Finley.

409
00:28:12,124 --> 00:28:15,185
What does he know about
explosives? He's no rocket scientist.

410
00:28:15,327 --> 00:28:17,296
He's lucky enough to
come in out of the rain.

411
00:28:17,429 --> 00:28:20,524
Well, he did a story on
some local demolition experts

412
00:28:20,666 --> 00:28:24,296
who hire out to the mob when
they're not doing construction.

413
00:28:24,436 --> 00:28:26,132
When was that?

414
00:28:26,271 --> 00:28:29,173
It never happened. They
didn't have any proof.

415
00:28:29,308 --> 00:28:31,174
- Got caught in the rain again, huh?
- Yeah.

416
00:28:31,310 --> 00:28:37,580
But the police think that Bill Finley hired
one of those guys to bomb Doug Levitt.

417
00:28:37,716 --> 00:28:39,412
Poor sucker.

418
00:28:39,551 --> 00:28:44,353
Well, Diane knew about the story.
It could just as easily have been her.

419
00:29:01,373 --> 00:29:03,433
What's Rapamune?

420
00:29:03,575 --> 00:29:06,238
Blood pressure medicine.
A lot of people take that.

421
00:29:07,980 --> 00:29:10,074
Now what?

422
00:29:10,215 --> 00:29:13,913
Well, we figure out which
demolition expert made that bomb

423
00:29:14,052 --> 00:29:17,511
and get him to say who
hired him in open court.

424
00:29:24,863 --> 00:29:27,833
Diane, how nice.

425
00:29:27,966 --> 00:29:29,195
Sit down, Nelson.

426
00:29:31,336 --> 00:29:32,827
Problems, Diane?

427
00:29:32,971 --> 00:29:36,100
Somebody's trying to
frame me for Doug's murder.

428
00:29:36,241 --> 00:29:39,234
Diane, come on. They
arrested Bill Finley.

429
00:29:39,378 --> 00:29:40,607
Who would want to frame you?

430
00:29:40,746 --> 00:29:43,614
I don't know, but somebody does.

431
00:29:43,749 --> 00:29:45,445
Ben Matlock came to see me.

432
00:29:45,584 --> 00:29:47,644
Yeah, me, too.
And he got nowhere.

433
00:29:47,786 --> 00:29:49,152
Relax.

434
00:29:49,288 --> 00:29:51,086
I want my money, Nelson.

435
00:29:51,223 --> 00:29:52,418
You'll get it.

436
00:29:52,557 --> 00:29:54,685
I want it by the
end of the week.

437
00:29:54,826 --> 00:29:57,159
And I want Doug's cut, too.

438
00:29:57,296 --> 00:29:59,288
Excuse me?

439
00:30:00,532 --> 00:30:02,865
Doug's cut.

440
00:30:03,001 --> 00:30:05,197
Or what? You'll
go to the police?

441
00:30:05,337 --> 00:30:07,397
You truly are out of your mind.

442
00:30:07,539 --> 00:30:08,899
I don't like being
framed, Nelson.

443
00:30:09,007 --> 00:30:12,842
If that money isn't in my
account in Bermuda by Friday...

444
00:30:14,913 --> 00:30:16,575
you're not going to
like it much, either.

445
00:30:20,052 --> 00:30:23,022
N-No, Conrad. Not from there.

446
00:30:23,155 --> 00:30:25,522
You can see the
sign fine from there.

447
00:30:25,657 --> 00:30:28,593
You've got to get
back where I was.

448
00:30:30,996 --> 00:30:34,330
You're too close. You've
got to get farther in the street.

449
00:30:34,466 --> 00:30:36,799
I can see the sign fine.

450
00:30:36,935 --> 00:30:38,369
You want to shoot this yourself?

451
00:30:38,503 --> 00:30:41,063
Just back up. Just
back... back on up.

452
00:30:41,206 --> 00:30:45,769
Just back... back up
till... Okay. Go on, back.

453
00:30:45,911 --> 00:30:47,345
Back, back, back.

454
00:30:47,479 --> 00:30:49,573
- Back up.
- Whoa!

455
00:30:59,591 --> 00:31:00,718
Did you hurt yourself?

456
00:31:00,859 --> 00:31:03,124
Sure I hurt myself. You
think I fell down for fun?

457
00:31:03,261 --> 00:31:05,821
Rub it a little. You'll recover.

458
00:31:05,964 --> 00:31:07,956
- You're not hurt that bad.
- How do you know?

459
00:31:08,100 --> 00:31:09,227
I'm a doctor.

460
00:31:09,368 --> 00:31:10,700
How much did it cost?

461
00:31:10,836 --> 00:31:12,065
None of your business.

462
00:31:12,204 --> 00:31:14,364
Well why are you going
through all this trouble anyway?

463
00:31:14,439 --> 00:31:16,601
I told you, it's the principle.

464
00:31:18,977 --> 00:31:20,502
The 8-year-old was wounded

465
00:31:20,645 --> 00:31:23,513
when a bullet passed through the
open window of the car driving by

466
00:31:23,648 --> 00:31:25,116
and struck him in the chest.

467
00:31:25,250 --> 00:31:28,709
He was taken to Children's Hospital
and is in satisfactory condition.

468
00:31:28,854 --> 00:31:32,188
None of the gang members involved
in the incident have been apprehended.

469
00:31:32,324 --> 00:31:37,353
When we return, a look at the early morning
fire that destroyed an Atlanta landmark.

470
00:31:37,496 --> 00:31:38,496
Stay with us.

471
00:31:38,563 --> 00:31:40,555
And we're clear.

472
00:31:40,699 --> 00:31:42,099
30 seconds, people.

473
00:31:42,234 --> 00:31:43,811
Where's that new copy?
Rob, Rob, Rob, Rob, Rob.

474
00:31:43,835 --> 00:31:46,031
- How's it going, Diane?
- Hi, Bill. How are you doing?

475
00:31:46,171 --> 00:31:49,141
Not too well, actually. Being
framed for murder is real pain.

476
00:31:49,274 --> 00:31:51,552
- Why did you do it anyway?
- What are you talking about, Bill?

477
00:31:51,576 --> 00:31:52,656
Fifteen seconds.

478
00:31:52,778 --> 00:31:55,418
I know about that press release,
Diane. What I want to know is why.

479
00:31:55,447 --> 00:31:56,967
Bill, I did not dummy
up that release.

480
00:31:57,082 --> 00:31:59,193
I don't know what to know is what
that form was doing in my office.

481
00:31:59,217 --> 00:32:01,017
Stop lying, okay? Why
did you kill him, Diane?

482
00:32:01,153 --> 00:32:02,644
What was going on
between you two?

483
00:32:02,788 --> 00:32:04,098
- Somebody please get him out of here.
- 10 seconds.

484
00:32:04,122 --> 00:32:05,814
I'm not leaving here
until I get the truth.

485
00:32:05,838 --> 00:32:06,868
Get your hands off of me.

486
00:32:06,892 --> 00:32:09,361
- Five seconds.
- For God's sakes, get Howard!

487
00:32:09,494 --> 00:32:12,388
Somebody, get... Two seconds.

488
00:32:14,132 --> 00:32:17,364
The Peachtree Museum was
the scene of a three-alarm fire

489
00:32:17,502 --> 00:32:20,165
which broke out about
4:30 this morning.

490
00:33:19,297 --> 00:33:21,095
You're right on time.

491
00:33:21,233 --> 00:33:23,134
- Do you like my suit?
- Yeah.

492
00:33:24,736 --> 00:33:26,671
- Everything under control?
- Yes, it is.

493
00:33:26,805 --> 00:33:29,673
Yeah, Ben, I followed
Addleson down to Southgate.

494
00:33:29,808 --> 00:33:31,333
Something's going on.

495
00:33:31,476 --> 00:33:32,876
Okay, I've got to go.

496
00:33:52,631 --> 00:33:54,691
Gentlemen, it's payday.

497
00:33:54,833 --> 00:33:57,962
Ha ha! Yeah! Give it up,
then, Reg. What's up, man?

498
00:33:58,103 --> 00:33:59,547
- I've been waiting for this.
- Give it up, man.

499
00:33:59,571 --> 00:34:01,802
- Yeah, yeah.
- Thank you, y'all.

500
00:34:01,940 --> 00:34:03,772
They know I had to be paid.

501
00:34:03,909 --> 00:34:06,936
All I want to know is what they
were saying before it worked.

502
00:34:07,078 --> 00:34:09,138
- They know I had to be paid.
- Uh-huh.

503
00:34:09,281 --> 00:34:11,216
<i>Oye.</i>

504
00:34:13,084 --> 00:34:14,404
- What's up, man?
- Hey, hey, hey.

505
00:34:14,486 --> 00:34:15,681
Shut up.

506
00:34:15,820 --> 00:34:18,312
- Don't be stupid, man.
- Yo, what's up, man?

507
00:34:18,456 --> 00:34:20,425
My brother got cut last night.

508
00:34:20,559 --> 00:34:22,255
Did he say it was us?

509
00:34:22,394 --> 00:34:23,692
He can't. You cut his throat.

510
00:34:27,499 --> 00:34:29,468
It wasn't us.

511
00:34:29,601 --> 00:34:30,660
I say it was.

512
00:34:30,802 --> 00:34:34,000
Wait a minute. He didn't kill
nobody. He was in jail last night.

513
00:34:34,139 --> 00:34:35,368
Everybody knew that, right?

514
00:34:35,507 --> 00:34:38,341
What's up, man?
He was in there, man.

515
00:34:41,846 --> 00:34:44,941
If my brother dies,
one of you dies.

516
00:34:45,083 --> 00:34:49,453
- Yeah, right.
- The exact same way.

517
00:35:01,866 --> 00:35:03,892
Yo, man, what's
the problem, man?

518
00:35:13,745 --> 00:35:15,270
Ben, guess what I found out.

519
00:35:15,413 --> 00:35:17,041
Howard Price called.

520
00:35:17,182 --> 00:35:18,878
Didn't I tell you
I'd handle this?

521
00:35:19,017 --> 00:35:21,418
- Yes.
- Then why did you down to that station

522
00:35:21,553 --> 00:35:24,921
and make an even bigger jackass
out of yourself than you already are?

523
00:35:25,056 --> 00:35:25,819
Ben, shut up.

524
00:35:25,957 --> 00:35:27,482
She wasn't there.

525
00:35:27,626 --> 00:35:28,924
Who wasn't where?

526
00:35:29,060 --> 00:35:30,995
Diane wasn't in her office.

527
00:35:31,129 --> 00:35:32,825
She doesn't have
an alibi after all.

528
00:35:42,741 --> 00:35:44,175
Chinese food?

529
00:35:44,309 --> 00:35:45,470
Yeah. Yeah.

530
00:35:45,610 --> 00:35:49,479
You ordered Chinese food from your
office the afternoon Doug was killed,

531
00:35:49,614 --> 00:35:52,365
but when the boy
tried to deliver it at

532
00:35:52,389 --> 00:35:55,520
3:25, he couldn't
because you weren't there.

533
00:35:55,654 --> 00:35:58,749
I did not order
Chinese food that day.

534
00:35:58,890 --> 00:36:03,351
Yes, you did because one of the fellows
that works down at the station remembers

535
00:36:03,495 --> 00:36:06,761
because when you weren't
there to accept the delivery, he did.

536
00:36:06,898 --> 00:36:10,733
Mr. Matlock, if I did, as you
contend, slip out of my office

537
00:36:10,869 --> 00:36:14,806
so I could drive up to Sidney
Lake and blow Doug to smithereens,

538
00:36:14,939 --> 00:36:18,774
why in God's name would I
have ordered Chinese food?

539
00:36:18,910 --> 00:36:24,406
Well, my guess is that you figured
you'd be back before it was delivered.

540
00:36:24,549 --> 00:36:28,418
And if it had worked, it would
have been a good idea, but it didn't.

541
00:36:29,621 --> 00:36:30,861
I've got to get ready for work.

542
00:36:30,922 --> 00:36:32,447
Here's your paper.

543
00:36:32,590 --> 00:36:33,614
Thank you very much.

544
00:36:33,758 --> 00:36:36,455
Oh, and your subpoena.

545
00:36:36,594 --> 00:36:37,618
Yeah.

546
00:37:17,569 --> 00:37:18,569
How are you?

547
00:37:18,703 --> 00:37:20,262
I didn't mean to scare you.

548
00:37:20,405 --> 00:37:21,405
Who are you?

549
00:37:21,473 --> 00:37:22,668
Conrad McMasters.

550
00:37:22,807 --> 00:37:24,537
I work for Ben
Matlock, the attorney.

551
00:37:24,676 --> 00:37:26,235
I want to ask you
some questions.

552
00:37:26,377 --> 00:37:27,504
About?

553
00:37:29,380 --> 00:37:31,380
Do you mind my asking
what you're working on there?

554
00:37:35,120 --> 00:37:36,782
A birdhouse.

555
00:37:39,791 --> 00:37:43,284
In view of how you make your living,
you can understand why I had to ask.

556
00:37:43,428 --> 00:37:44,988
I don't know what
you're talking about.

557
00:37:45,063 --> 00:37:48,431
I'm investigating the explosion
that killed Doug Levitt last week,

558
00:37:48,566 --> 00:37:51,078
and I have reason to believe that
you're the one that rigged the bomb.

559
00:37:51,102 --> 00:37:53,469
The police have
already been here.

560
00:37:53,605 --> 00:37:56,040
They didn't get anywhere,
and neither will you.

561
00:37:56,174 --> 00:37:59,076
Yeah, but they don't
know who hired you. I do...

562
00:37:59,210 --> 00:38:00,210
Diane Becker.

563
00:38:01,980 --> 00:38:03,107
Never heard of her.

564
00:38:03,248 --> 00:38:05,774
I understand usually in these
jobs you just blow up property,

565
00:38:05,917 --> 00:38:07,180
but here somebody died.

566
00:38:07,318 --> 00:38:09,253
You're talking
about an accident.

567
00:38:09,387 --> 00:38:11,185
I'm talking about murder.

568
00:38:13,858 --> 00:38:15,156
What? Diane didn't tell you

569
00:38:15,293 --> 00:38:17,037
that somebody was in that
cottage when you blew it up?

570
00:38:17,061 --> 00:38:20,361
Nobody's ever died in any of
your explosions before, Mr. Krauss.

571
00:38:20,498 --> 00:38:21,898
She lied to you, didn't she?

572
00:38:22,033 --> 00:38:24,873
I don't know what you're talking
about, and that's all I'm going to say.

573
00:38:25,003 --> 00:38:26,266
Now get out.

574
00:38:54,766 --> 00:38:56,496
Hello.

575
00:38:56,634 --> 00:38:58,603
<i>You were right.</i>

576
00:38:58,736 --> 00:39:00,227
<i>She did lie to me.</i>

577
00:39:01,873 --> 00:39:04,104
The more I think about
it, the madder I get.

578
00:39:04,242 --> 00:39:05,505
So you listen up.

579
00:39:07,378 --> 00:39:08,402
I'm listening.

580
00:39:08,546 --> 00:39:12,745
I didn't push the
button. She did.

581
00:39:12,884 --> 00:39:14,318
I always do it that way.

582
00:39:15,420 --> 00:39:20,381
I rig the explosives, and I
order a detonator from a buddy.

583
00:39:20,525 --> 00:39:23,188
The client picks
it up and uses it.

584
00:39:23,328 --> 00:39:26,321
It's safer for me that way.

585
00:39:26,464 --> 00:39:32,563
Now I'm going to give you my
buddy's name, and I'm going to hang up.

586
00:39:32,704 --> 00:39:35,173
Then I'm going
on a long vacation.

587
00:39:36,174 --> 00:39:37,506
All right. Hang on.

588
00:39:39,010 --> 00:39:40,069
Go ahead.

589
00:39:45,116 --> 00:39:49,645
Uh, do you recognize
this, Ms. Becker?

590
00:39:49,787 --> 00:39:53,747
Of course. It's the device that
triggered the bomb that killed Doug Levitt.

591
00:39:53,892 --> 00:39:55,827
The police found it
in Mr. Finley's garage.

592
00:39:55,960 --> 00:39:58,225
I watched the assistant
D.A. enter it into evidence.

593
00:39:58,363 --> 00:40:00,764
Did you see it before that?

594
00:40:00,899 --> 00:40:02,265
No, of course not.

595
00:40:02,400 --> 00:40:03,527
No?

596
00:40:03,668 --> 00:40:06,536
Isn't this the device you
bought from Jake Lubenthal?

597
00:40:07,805 --> 00:40:09,103
Excuse me?

598
00:40:09,240 --> 00:40:11,766
You do know Jake
Lubenthal, don't you?

599
00:40:11,910 --> 00:40:13,708
I've never heard of him.

600
00:40:13,845 --> 00:40:15,370
Well, he knows you.

601
00:40:15,513 --> 00:40:18,608
Well, a lot of people know
me whom I don't know.

602
00:40:18,750 --> 00:40:19,750
Well, he does.

603
00:40:20,752 --> 00:40:22,345
Jake, stand up.

604
00:40:23,388 --> 00:40:25,721
There. See? Recognize him now?

605
00:40:25,857 --> 00:40:27,086
No.

606
00:40:27,225 --> 00:40:31,185
The reason I keep asking is that he
had a long talk with the judge this morning

607
00:40:31,329 --> 00:40:33,594
and with the assistant
district attorney,

608
00:40:33,731 --> 00:40:35,359
and he's been granted immunity.

609
00:40:35,500 --> 00:40:37,765
And that means when he
comes up here and testifies

610
00:40:37,902 --> 00:40:40,895
that he sold you this
detonator on March 25th,

611
00:40:41,039 --> 00:40:42,940
just two days before the murder,

612
00:40:43,074 --> 00:40:44,838
he won't be prosecuted
as an accessory.

613
00:40:44,976 --> 00:40:47,468
You bought this
from Jake Lubenthal

614
00:40:47,612 --> 00:40:50,275
and used it to set off the bomb
that was made by Trevor Krauss.

615
00:40:50,415 --> 00:40:53,112
You murdered Doug
Levitt, didn't you?

616
00:40:54,185 --> 00:40:57,622
Your Honor, uh, I'd just as soon
not answer any more questions

617
00:40:57,755 --> 00:40:59,485
until I've spoken
with my attorney.

618
00:40:59,624 --> 00:41:02,651
I object, Your Honor. She's
been sworn to tell the truth.

619
00:41:02,794 --> 00:41:04,626
Please direct her to
answer my question.

620
00:41:04,762 --> 00:41:06,424
Overruled, Mr. Matlock.

621
00:41:06,564 --> 00:41:09,056
The witness is entitled
to confer with counsel.

622
00:41:09,200 --> 00:41:13,865
This court will reconvene
tomorrow morning at 9:00 a.m.

623
00:41:23,281 --> 00:41:25,546
I'm a busy man. This
had better be good.

624
00:41:25,683 --> 00:41:27,743
One of your guys
shot an 8-year-old kid.

625
00:41:27,885 --> 00:41:30,684
Accident. It happens.

626
00:41:30,822 --> 00:41:32,984
This is the first and
the last accident.

627
00:41:33,124 --> 00:41:35,389
Injured bystanders
attract too much attention.

628
00:41:35,526 --> 00:41:36,526
Okay.

629
00:41:36,594 --> 00:41:37,994
No more gunplay.

630
00:41:38,129 --> 00:41:39,358
Okay!

631
00:41:45,203 --> 00:41:47,035
Still running that
scam with Reggie, huh?

632
00:41:47,171 --> 00:41:49,640
That's good. You're in
business, I'm in business.

633
00:41:49,774 --> 00:41:52,141
I don't know what the
hell you're talking about.

634
00:41:55,113 --> 00:41:56,113
Doug?

635
00:41:56,214 --> 00:41:58,080
That's right.

636
00:41:58,216 --> 00:42:00,208
Man, they found your body.

637
00:42:00,351 --> 00:42:03,150
No, just some poor old bum.

638
00:42:03,287 --> 00:42:04,846
You screwed up, Nelson.

639
00:42:04,989 --> 00:42:06,423
What do you mean?

640
00:42:06,557 --> 00:42:09,857
You don't expect me to believe that
Diane set me up all by herself, do you?

641
00:42:09,994 --> 00:42:11,895
Diane tried to kill you?

642
00:42:13,931 --> 00:42:15,991
I want my cut of that land
deal, and I want it now.

643
00:42:16,134 --> 00:42:17,932
I haven't got it. I
gave it to Diane.

644
00:42:18,069 --> 00:42:19,264
Why did you do that?

645
00:42:19,404 --> 00:42:22,203
Because she said she'd go to
the cops if I didn't give it to her.

646
00:42:25,043 --> 00:42:26,739
That's okay.
Diane's taken care of.

647
00:42:26,878 --> 00:42:28,278
What do you mean?

648
00:42:28,413 --> 00:42:30,314
I've been making her sweat.

649
00:42:30,448 --> 00:42:32,781
The cops will nail
her for my murder.

650
00:42:32,917 --> 00:42:34,783
I've been leaving little clues.

651
00:42:34,919 --> 00:42:36,387
You're the one?

652
00:42:36,521 --> 00:42:38,786
Yeah, I thought the Chinese
food was a nice touch.

653
00:42:38,923 --> 00:42:42,121
What are you, an idiot? If
she goes down, we all go down.

654
00:42:42,260 --> 00:42:46,027
I thought you were in on this
killing me business with Diane.

655
00:42:46,164 --> 00:42:47,393
- Are you stupid?
- It's okay.

656
00:42:47,532 --> 00:42:48,532
No, it's not okay.

657
00:42:48,666 --> 00:42:50,032
It's okay.

658
00:42:51,169 --> 00:42:53,138
I'll fix it.

659
00:42:55,473 --> 00:42:56,907
He'll fix it.

660
00:43:27,939 --> 00:43:29,339
Oh, man.

661
00:43:37,215 --> 00:43:38,649
- Diane.
- Oh!

662
00:43:40,651 --> 00:43:42,847
Doesn't death become me?

663
00:43:48,793 --> 00:43:51,092
No! No! No! No!

664
00:43:53,998 --> 00:44:01,337
When I saw those blank press releases
from the Atlanta Nature Society in here,

665
00:44:01,472 --> 00:44:03,168
I started to follow you.

666
00:44:03,307 --> 00:44:05,367
No! Ow!

667
00:44:08,412 --> 00:44:10,904
And when you met with that
guy at the construction site,

668
00:44:11,048 --> 00:44:15,144
I remembered that story we
investigated about the demolition scam.

669
00:44:15,286 --> 00:44:18,484
And suddenly it hit me, you
wanted me to meet you at the cottage

670
00:44:18,623 --> 00:44:20,558
so you could blow
me to kingdom come.

671
00:44:20,691 --> 00:44:24,651
Well, I hate to tell you, Diane,

672
00:44:24,795 --> 00:44:26,907
but the guy you killed was
just some poor old drifter.

673
00:44:26,931 --> 00:44:28,593
I'm still very much alive.

674
00:44:28,733 --> 00:44:30,565
What are you going to do?

675
00:44:30,701 --> 00:44:33,466
Well, the thing is, Diane,

676
00:44:33,604 --> 00:44:38,440
back then I was very angry with
you, so I started setting you up.

677
00:44:38,576 --> 00:44:39,976
Do you remember
the Chinese food?

678
00:44:40,111 --> 00:44:43,377
The blank press
releases in your office?

679
00:44:43,514 --> 00:44:45,346
That was you?

680
00:44:45,483 --> 00:44:46,678
Yeah.

681
00:44:48,319 --> 00:44:50,754
But I made a mistake, Diane.

682
00:44:50,888 --> 00:44:56,725
I forgot that the trail leads
from you to Nelson Addleson.

683
00:44:58,062 --> 00:45:03,831
And now that I'm dead, Nelson's
my sole source of support.

684
00:45:03,968 --> 00:45:07,530
If you talk, he goes
down, and so do I.

685
00:45:08,739 --> 00:45:10,731
I swear to God, I won't talk.

686
00:45:10,875 --> 00:45:12,104
I won't say a word.

687
00:45:12,243 --> 00:45:14,371
- Really? Really, Diane?
- Yeah.

688
00:45:14,512 --> 00:45:17,949
- I can trust you?
- You can trust me. You can trust me.

689
00:45:18,082 --> 00:45:23,077
I wish I could believe
that, but I don't.

690
00:45:25,056 --> 00:45:26,490
So you're going
to commit suicide.

691
00:45:28,826 --> 00:45:30,522
No one will hear you.

692
00:45:33,231 --> 00:45:35,166
It won't be bad.

693
00:45:35,299 --> 00:45:39,236
Oh, God, no! No! No!

694
00:45:39,370 --> 00:45:40,770
No!

695
00:45:48,546 --> 00:45:50,276
Sweet dreams, Diane.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
<font color="#ffff00" size=14>www.tvsubtitles.net</font>
